{"title":"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Generalized_Value_of_k)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Generalized Value of k)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Specified_Values_of_k)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Specified Values of k)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Simple_and_Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Simple and Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Using_Average_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Using Average Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Learning_Royal\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Learning Royal</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The quiz scores of a class with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ad30cf40f4cdcd2266dbc2c4df9e7a8e170a089.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> students have a mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The mean of a collection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of these quiz scores is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the mean of the remaining quiz scores in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/564ecd290d2759397ef0353eeddf6f99185e53d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~\\frac{14-8}{k-12} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~\\frac{8k-168}{k-12} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~\\frac{14}{12} - \\frac{8}{k} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~\\frac{14(k-12)}{k^2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~\\frac{14(k-12)}{8k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"661\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Generalized_Value_of_k.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Generalized_Value_of_k)\">Solution 1 (Generalized Value of k)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Generalized Value of k)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total score of the class is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acf7c5aa604c85704cfaf3f6bd643e9e5cd99c4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> and the total score of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> quizzes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a831a27277afade1d13d65e5316452dc9ad276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\cdot14=168.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />\nTherefore, for the remaining quizzes (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439bcf365ae2f6eb9529863cdb28a8da12bd4e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> of them), the total score is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/006c2890308756993ff6dd10e8ee97a3628a4f73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8k-168.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" /> Their mean score is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/300ed8d5cf535a747d484db387cad28bcbd5e173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} ~\\frac{8k-168}{k-12}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"121\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Specified_Values_of_k.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Specified_Values_of_k)\">Solution 2 (Specified Values of k)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Specified Values of k)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c57a060fb71f986140e17f0fcfd87b3ea5a0d4f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=13.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> The answer is the same as the last student's quiz score, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad8a1e3db56a4974d00cc060a1332d7b4e2300f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\cdot13-14\\cdot12&lt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"15\" /> From the answer choices, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726fe70f38dc8e4f990776b389279ca9c733ee78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} ~\\frac{8k-168}{k-12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"118\" height=\"50\" /> is negative at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c57a060fb71f986140e17f0fcfd87b3ea5a0d4f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=13.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You know that the mean of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e395ecfa661165ea0d06fc0114eb7c24f075ead7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> so that means all of them combined had a score of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa41287d2d9db9e9c5785f3946b588fe34ddcf9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\cdot14 = 168.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" /> Set the mean of the remaining students (in other words the value you are trying to solve for), to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> The total number of remaining students in a class of size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd27f53057b22d1ec68497c901cac42cc52d2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> The total score <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439bcf365ae2f6eb9529863cdb28a8da12bd4e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> students got combined can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d096f52bbd358857d700e8612a8f70204fd70189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(k-12),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> and the total score all of the students in the class got was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f608652cf5498adec76658108b188c158c0c9c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168 + a(k-12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> (the first twelve students, plus the remaining students). The mean of the whole class can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c452efcb1e0a7c2582a6d6aeaff118e6c5c32b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{168 + a(k-12)}{k}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"38\" /> The mean of the class has already been given as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a9fb4c5b23667e57f28d844ad99715f18ba3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> so by just writing the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf6adaf58590e4d8198600a2de35e83b1c1c523.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{168 + a(k-12)}{k} = 8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" /> and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (the mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439bcf365ae2f6eb9529863cdb28a8da12bd4e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> students) will give you the answer in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99a6aaebc17474bd09ea71d84d4e769a0662b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/300ed8d5cf535a747d484db387cad28bcbd5e173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} ~\\frac{8k-168}{k-12}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"121\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~Ankitamc (Solution)\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> Adjustments)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Simple_and_Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Simple_and_Quick)\">Video Solution (Simple and Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Simple and Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/STPoBU6A3yU\">https://youtu.be/STPoBU6A3yU</a>\n</p><p>~ Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S4q1ji013JQ&amp;list=PLexHyfQ8DMuKqltG3cHT7Di4jhVl6L4YJ&amp;index=5\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S4q1ji013JQ&amp;list=PLexHyfQ8DMuKqltG3cHT7Di4jhVl6L4YJ&amp;index=5</a>\n</p><p>~ North America Math Contest Go Go Go\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Using_Average_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Using_Average_Formula)\">Video Solution (Using Average Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Using Average Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jocfZVNGU3o\">https://youtu.be/jocfZVNGU3o</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wacb0roj20A\">https://youtu.be/wacb0roj20A</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/50CThrk3RcM/t=399\">https://youtu.be/50CThrk3RcM/t=399</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Learning_Royal\">Video Solution by The Learning Royal</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by The Learning Royal\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/slVBYmcDMOI\">https://youtu.be/slVBYmcDMOI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width